    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8086" root="حشد" body-key="H">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَاشِدٌ</span></b>  [A people <i>collecting themselves together,</i>
or <i>assembling,</i> &amp;c. (see 1)]: pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حُشَّدٌ</span>, occurring
in a trad., followed by <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وُفَّدٌ</span>. (L.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَآءَ فُلَانٌ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَافِلًا حَاشِدًا</span> and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُحْتَفِلًا مُحْتَشِدًا</span></b>  <i>Such a one
came</i> [<i>full of energy,</i>] <i>prepared, furnished, equipped,</i> or <i>accoutred.</i> (S.) See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَشِدٌ</span>.

